{
  "description": "Future time limit vectors. A header's timestamp t is accepted iff t > mtpPrev and t <= maxTime, where mtpPrev is the median time past of the parent of the block being validated and maxTime = MaxTime(mtpPrev, now): now + 7200 if the 2027 rules are not yet active on the parent; otherwise min(now + 7200, mtpPrev + 1) if mtpPrev > now + 720; otherwise now + 720. `now` is the validating node's own clock in Unix seconds, never adjusted by peer reports; it is an input here. `height` is the block being validated and `activationHeight` is H_a: the rules are active on the parent, and the last two arms apply, iff height >= H_a + 1 (`rulesActiveOnParent`). `mtpPrevMinusNow` and `maxTimeMinusNow` restate mtpPrev and maxTime relative to the clock. `validTimestamps` is the number of timestamps that pass, the size of (mtpPrev, maxTime], zero when the chain cannot be extended at this clock reading. Each entry of `probes` is one timestamp `time` (with `timeMinusNow`) and whether a header carrying it is `valid`. Times in the vectors are JSON integers in seconds; heights and constants are decimal strings.",
  "constants": {
    "LEGACY_MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME": "7200",
